Fix nix-update evaluating a flake source that Nix never materialised.

`nix flake metadata --json` reports the content-addressed store path a local
flake source would get, and up to Nix 2.34 that path was written to the store
as a side effect of the call. Nix 2.35 dropped the copy (NixOS/nix#15711), so
the path is reported but nothing exists there and evaluating
`builtins.getFlake <store path>` dies with

    error: opening file "/nix/store/...-source": No such file or directory

Report "no store path" when the path is missing; the callers (eval.nix and the
prefetchers) already treat None as "evaluate the local directory".

diff --git a/nix_update/options.py b/nix_update/options.py
--- a/nix_update/options.py
+++ b/nix_update/options.py
@@ -122,9 +122,13 @@
 
         flake_dir = _metadata_flake_dir(metadata)
         if flake_dir:
-            return str(Path(path) / flake_dir)
+            path = str(Path(path) / flake_dir)
     except (subprocess.CalledProcessError, json.JSONDecodeError):
         return None
+    # Nix >= 2.35 copies flake sources lazily, so the reported path may never
+    # have been written. Callers treat None as "evaluate the directory".
+    if not Path(path).exists():
+        return None
     return path
 
 
